{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS3159CwtyjyfNM3Jd6P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014fskiKxw4W8PjHEF79mv3L","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-Ea3DRY/ANSWER.md","content":"# ANSWER\n\n## Changes\nNone. I did not change `gen.py`, because I can't verify a fix from this repo.\n\n## What the evidence shows\n- `gen.py` emits what the plan says: `hr: {units: \"%lthr\", value: lo, end: hi}`.\n  The readback (`event-184233-as-sent.json`) matches that exactly, so the generator isn't mangling the plan.\n- The clamping happens after the API accepts the event. Intervals.icu exports `%lthr` targets to Garmin\n  as the watch's own HR zones, so the watch shows zone bands (118–137, 151–162, ...). Re-setting the\n  watch LTHR only moves those bands, which fits this.\n- Both alternatives already tried fail for different reasons:\n  - `units: \"bpm\"` gave 214–249, so the values were scaled or interpreted differently from what we sent.\n  - `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` gave a constant 101, so those aren't fields the doc schema reads.\n\n## Why I stopped\nThe fix is probably to send absolute bpm in a form that Intervals exports as a custom range\n(for example, converting `hr_pct × 172` in `gen.py` and using the correct units key). I don't know\nthe right schema key or units string, though. Nothing in the repo documents it, and I'm not allowed to\ncall the API to test. A guess would be a fourth failed attempt on a real event.\n\n## Suggested next step\n1. Check the Intervals.icu API docs, or create one workout in the UI with a custom bpm range\n   (e.g. 151–160 bpm). Then `GET` that event and copy the `workout_doc` shape it returns.\n2. Make `hr_target()` in `gen.py` produce that shape, with bpm = round(pct/100 × LTHR). LTHR (172)\n   would need to be a plan field or a CLI argument.\n3. Check the result on the watch (expected: 117–129, 151–160, 129–141, 112–124).\n\nIf you give me that readback or a doc link, I can make the change.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1645,"cache_read_input_tokens":21025,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1645},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e84dc486-3da9-4b1c-96eb-efe940eb92f9","uuid":"b7e963ea-2587-4f8a-86cc-fcd8a846030e","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:31:11.888Z","request_id":"req_011CgS314t6AfuP5ze5KRQeP","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014fskiKxw4W8PjHEF79mv3L":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-Ea3DRY/ANSWER.md","content":"# ANSWER\n\n## Changes\nNone. I did not change `gen.py`, because I can't verify a fix from this repo.\n\n## What the evidence shows\n- `gen.py` emits what the plan says: `hr: {units: \"%lthr\", value: lo, end: hi}`.\n  The readback (`event-184233-as-sent.json`) matches that exactly, so the generator isn't mangling the plan.\n- The clamping happens after the API accepts the event. Intervals.icu exports `%lthr` targets to Garmin\n  as the watch's own HR zones, so the watch shows zone bands (118–137, 151–162, ...). Re-setting the\n  watch LTHR only moves those bands, which fits this.\n- Both alternatives already tried fail for different reasons:\n  - `units: \"bpm\"` gave 214–249, so the values were scaled or interpreted differently from what we sent.\n  - `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` gave a constant 101, so those aren't fields the doc schema reads.\n\n## Why I stopped\nThe fix is probably to send absolute bpm in a form that Intervals exports as a custom range\n(for example, converting `hr_pct × 172` in `gen.py` and using the correct units key). I don't know\nthe right schema key or units string, though. Nothing in the repo documents it, and I'm not allowed to\ncall the API to test. A guess would be a fourth failed attempt on a real event.\n\n## Suggested next step\n1. Check the Intervals.icu API docs, or create one workout in the UI with a custom bpm range\n   (e.g. 151–160 bpm). Then `GET` that event and copy the `workout_doc` shape it returns.\n2. Make `hr_target()` in `gen.py` produce that shape, with bpm = round(pct/100 × LTHR). LTHR (172)\n   would need to be a plan field or a CLI argument.\n3. Check the result on the watch (expected: 117–129, 151–160, 129–141, 112–124).\n\nIf you give me that readback or a doc link, I can make the change.\n"}}}
